cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "This repository and its released research artifacts are citable; the current manuscript is a working draft and should not yet be cited as a final paper."
title: "Synthetic Players: auditable strategic experiments with LLM-controlled agents"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nakajima
    given-names: Yohei
repository-code: "https://github.com/yoheinakajima/synthetic-players"
license: MIT
version: "phase5-review-v6"
date-released: "2026-07-29"
abstract: >-
  An open research program on LLM-controlled agents in strategic games,
  including externally anchored registrations, event-sourced execution,
  mechanical adjudication, behavioral drift monitoring, byte-exact replay,
  and public post-adjudication sensitivity analyses. The current paper studies
  a fixed panel of lightweight persona prompts that passes coarse marginal
  checks while producing small continuation-probability point estimates with
  wide dependence-aware intervals. Corrected estimates assign most episode-level variation to
  differences between prompt configurations. The repository does not claim
  human substitutability, and published human references are protocol-nonmatched.
keywords:
  - behavioral game theory
  - large language models
  - LLM social simulation
  - synthetic participants
  - persona prompting
  - preregistration
  - computational reproducibility
  - mechanical adjudication
  - causal validation
